From c4b35106e91f582dce7e47ca269005cfdb69c13c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Dec 2023 10:48:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 716/913] core: plat-stm32mp1: properly encapsulate pager code
 with CFG_WITH_PAGER

Encapsulate all internal RAM management code, that is pager specific,
with CFG_WITH_PAGER.

While there, correct an #endif comment

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git cfe37220f0213ef0988057f0bb6408e71073ce3d core: plat-stm32mp1: properly encapsulate pager code with CFG_WITH_PAGER]
Change-Id: I7737bb248af371fa3581d202fd0d3fd03a328e2e
Signed-off-by: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/main.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/main.c
index f131a5274..2c27a547c 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/main.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/main.c
@@ -183,6 +183,7 @@ void boot_secondary_init_intc(void)
 		   RCC_MP_RSTSCLRR_MPUP1RSTF);
 }
 
+#ifdef CFG_WITH_PAGER
 /*
  * This concerns OP-TEE pager for STM32MP1 to use secure internal
  * RAMs to execute. TZSRAM refers the TZSRAM_BASE/TZSRAM_SIZE
@@ -250,7 +251,6 @@ void boot_secondary_init_intc(void)
 
 #define TZSRAM_IS_IN_DRAM	(CFG_TZSRAM_START >= CFG_DRAM_BASE)
 
-#ifdef CFG_WITH_PAGER
 /*
  * At build time, we enforce that, when pager is used,
  * either TZSRAM fully fits inside SYSRAM secure address range,
-- 
